these are the last remaining ukrainian  fighters in the azov stall steel plant  now they are prisoners of war  they survived russia's onslaught for  more than two months in the steel plant  their future is now unknown their  surrender brings a much needed victory  for russian forces in the strategically  important port city of mariopol  the minister of defence has reported to  presidents of russia on the end of the  operation and the complete liberation of  the azov style industrial complex and of  the city of mariopol from ukrainian  fighters  the kremlin says those who've  surrendered will be treated in line with  international norms some russian  lawmakers have demanded they be tried  for war crimes and one said they should  face the death penalty  sergey shoigu announced his forces  alongside russian-backed separatists  will soon claim full control over the  lugansk region in eastern ukraine  a victory that's long overdue for his  forces  forces the defense minister wants to  expand  he revealed plans for 12 more military  units to be added to the military  districts in western russia in response  to finland and sweden applying to join  nato  that expansion needs more manpower and  the russian lawmakers may have the  solution the state duma on friday said  it's considering a bill that would allow  russians over the age of 40 and  foreigners over the age of 30 to sign up  for the military  the website of the russian parliament's  lower house the state duma said the move  would enable the military to utilize the  skills of older professionals familiar  with the use of high precision weapons  and military equipment  as what russia calls its special  military operation nears the three-month  mark there is no indication from either  side of an end to the conflict  dorsochapari al jazeera moscow
 

